<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28800" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mergus</span></b> , i, m.
		mergo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A diver</i>, a kind of water-fowl, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 78</span></i>
			Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praesagiunt pluviam mergi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 35, 87, § 362</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mergi maria fugientes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
				ib.</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8, 625</span></i>; cf.: aequor amat; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomenque tenet, quia mergitur illo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 11, 795</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hor. Epod. 10, 22</span></i>.—Jestingly: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mergus agrarius, of one who is eager to possess
					lands,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Capitol. Pertin. 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A vine-layer</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 4, 15,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pall. 3, 16, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
